@* A line of the properties panel that may say a failure (row 37 of the queue, the rule of row 29 for
   the whole panel): one plain sentence, and what came back - the problem document with its status,
   title, detail and trace id, or the failure's own type and message - behind a "?" at its right
   (DrawioHelp, the panel's own way of keeping text off screen and at hand: its heading and its mission
   steps have one). The row under the bar's "Details" opens a window from a line of that row, and this
   sentence is not one; a note beside it keeps the answer next to what it explains. Shut, it is hidden,
   not removed, so it can still be read by its id: the "?" is {Id}-help and the answer {Id}-detail.
   A line with nothing behind it is the paragraph it always was, without the row around it; with
   something behind it, the line's own place in the dock (LineClass: an outcome's rule above it, its
   room at the foot) goes to the row, so that the rule runs over the "?" too. The panel's lines that
   come from code other windows share - the edit permit that could not be asked for, a command's
   outcome, the label the drawing did not take - are said so in those windows too (the owner's answer
   of 9/10): the save, the creation, the engine's band, the device list, Operations, PLC connections.
   Since the owner's answer of 10/10 every failure line of the page is: the checks' configuration
   check and "go to", the missions, the junction list's "go to" too. *@
@if (Detail is null)
{
    <p id="@Id" class="@Joined(LineClass, Class)">@Text</p>
}
else
{
    <div class="@Joined("drawio-failure-line", LineClass)">
        <p id="@Id" class="@Class">@Text</p>
        <DrawioHelp Id="@($"{Id}-help")" Label="Technical detail of the failure">
            <p id="@($"{Id}-detail")" class="drawio-failure-detail">@Detail</p>
        </DrawioHelp>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The sentence's id; the "?" is <c>{Id}-help</c>, what came back <c>{Id}-detail</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Id { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>The sentence's classes - the panel's error red, an outcome's place at the foot of the dock.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Where the line sits in the dock (<c>drawio-property-outcome</c>): on the row when there is a "?", on the sentence when there is not.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? LineClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Text { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>What came back, behind the "?"; null for a line that says no failed request.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Detail { get; set; }

    private static string Joined(string? first, string? second) =>
        string.Join(' ', new[] { first, second }.Where(part => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(part)));
}
